110 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 48 0 R
/T (VLAN \(Virtual LAN\): a way to logically partition a single physical switch \(or set of switches\) into multiple separate broadcast domains, without needing separate physical switches per department. Each port on a switch is assigned to a VLAN \(e.g., VLAN 10 = HR, VLAN 20 = Finance\). Devices in the same VLAN can communicate directly at Layer 2; devices in different VLANs cannot, even if plugged into the same physical switch, until something routes between them. )
/E (VLAN \(Virtual LAN\): a way to logically partition a single physical switch \(or set of switches\) into multiple separate broadcast domains, without needing separate physical switches per department. Each port on a switch is assigned to a VLAN \(e.g., VLAN 10 = HR, VLAN 20 = Finance\). Devices in the same VLAN can communicate directly at Layer 2; devices in different VLANs cannot, even if plugged into the same physical switch, until something routes between them. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
